    turnFlow: "1. **Auction**: Players bid for contracts (e.g., 'Boston' for 8 tricks, 'Petit Misère' for zero). 2. **Trump**: The suit of the turned-up card from the second deck usually determines the 'preference' suit for trumps. 3. **The Play**: Standard trick-taking rules. Must follow suit. 4. **Tricks**: Highest trump wins; else highest card of led suit wins.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Boston is a point-based trick-taking game and does not utilize a monetary or chip-based ante system.',
      deal: 'The initial distribution of thirteen cards to each player is handled automatically by the system dealer.',
      reveal_market: 'This is a closed-hand bidding game where all cards are dealt; no community market or shared cards exist.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external area; they must play with their original hand.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire deck is distributed at the start of the round; no cards remain in stock to be purchased.',
      fold: 'Participation is mandatory for every trick to determine if the declarer meets their bid requirement.',
      check: 'The game uses a trick-taking and bidding structure rather than a vying structure where checking would apply.',
      call: 'There is no bet to match in this game; competition is based on contract levels and trick wins.',
      bet: 'Success is measured by points on a complex scoring table rather than through direct financial betting.',
      raise: 'Contract levels are increased during the auction phase via bidding rather than through wagering rounds.',
      declare: 'The auction result defines the contract; no separate declaration phase exists during the actual card play.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands stay private until cards are played into tricks; no full-hand reveal phase occurs in the game.',
      award_pot: 'Winning points are calculated based on the scoring table and awarded from other players rather than a pot.',
      play_card: 'Must follow suit; highest trump or highest led card wins.',
      draw: 'Each player receives thirteen cards at the start and no further drawing occurs during the play phase.',
      discard: 'Every card in the hand must be played into a trick; no cards are discarded to a waste pile.',
      pass: 'Allowed at any time during the bidding phase.',
      bid: 'Must exceed the current bid in the hierarchy of contracts.',
      meld: 'Boston is a trick-taking game based on counts rather than forming sequences or melds.',
      go_out: 'The hand terminates automatically once all thirteen tricks have been played by all participants.',
